Call site of the interface method ctx.Err(). The context implementations return the
error stored in the context (context.Canceled / DeadlineExceeded are stored by
cancel), so the expected result is an explicit Unresolved(memory) entry inside
context/context.go reached through a dynamic hop; a 0-entry set would be a silent
drop. The sentinels themselves are not expected to be resolved.
-- args --
jobs/jobs.go:@ctxerr
